\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces Fabrication worklow of a Laser-Written Vapor Cell. Steps (1-2) describe the FLICE process. In step (4) NEG dispenser placement and bonding are performed. Activation is illustrated by step (5). From \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {lucivero2022}.}}{5}{figure.caption.6}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.2}{\ignorespaces Laser-Written Vapor Cell manufactured using the FLICE technique. It consists of a cylindrical reservoir (5~mm diameter, 3.5~mm height) connected to a rectangular parallelepiped sensing channel ($1 \times 1$~mm cross-section, 9.5~mm length). From \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {lucivero2022}}}{9}{figure.caption.11}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.3}{\ignorespaces Hydroxyl radicals formation upon the decomposition of Caro's acid in Piranha solution. From \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {caro2017}.}}{13}{figure.caption.20}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.4}{\ignorespaces Schematic representation of a hydroxylated/hydrophilic surface. From \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {kern1993}.}}{14}{figure.caption.21}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.5}{\ignorespaces Schematic representation of a contaminant being lifted from a quartz surface due to the Zeta potential. Adapted from \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {lin2012}.}}{14}{figure.caption.23}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.6}{\ignorespaces Effects of plasma treatment on silica surfaces. Plasma removes contaminants and increases the density of available silanol groups. Adapted from \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {yu2023}.}}{16}{figure.caption.27}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.7}{\ignorespaces Evolution of bonding energy with annealing time. Bond strength follows a logarithmic growth law; annealing reduces the characteristic time constant $\mu $, accelerating convergence toward the bulk fracture energy. From \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {cho2001}.}}{18}{figure.caption.28}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.8}{\ignorespaces Effect of applied pressure on the bonding process. Forces perpendicular to the interface suppress void formation by closing residual gaps between surface asperities. From \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {mai2015}.}}{19}{figure.caption.29}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.9}{\ignorespaces Pressure plate geometry described by Birckigt et al.\ \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {birckigt2021}. The curved profiles guide contact front propagation outward from the center, reducing the probability of interface void formation.}}{19}{figure.caption.30}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.10}{\ignorespaces Comparison of the permeability constant $K$ across uncoated borofloat, uncoated aluminosilicate, Al$_{2}$O$_{3}$-coated borofloat, and Al$_{2}$O$_{3}$-coated aluminosilicate glasses. From \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {carle2023}.}}{20}{figure.caption.31}%
